1:1 COMMENT "# generator_chain.z -- composing generators by driving one from"
1:64 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "# inside another."
2:18 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "#"
3:2 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# Two `IntRange` iterators are concatenated by an outer generator"
4:66 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# `Chained` that drives each in turn. The inline form"
5:54 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# `for x: (IntRange ...) loop { yield x }` works because a for-loop"
6:68 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "# iterable that is a construction is hoisted to a temp before the"
7:66 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "# loop -- and that temp crosses the enclosing generator's"
8:58 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# suspensions, so it is promoted to a field of `Chained` and"
9:61 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "# persists across `.call` invocations."
10:39 EOL "\n"
11:1 COMMENT "#"
11:2 EOL "\n"
12:1 COMMENT "# Equivalent explicit-binding form:"
12:36 EOL "\n"
13:1 COMMENT "#   inner1: (IntRange lo: this.a_lo hi: this.a_hi)"
13:51 EOL "\n"
14:1 COMMENT "#   for x: inner1 loop { yield x }"
14:35 EOL "\n"
15:1 COMMENT "# (named local, same outcome; the spec lists both forms.)"
15:58 EOL "\n"
16:1 EOL "\n"
